      "text": "7D–F: 3. There is a famous vase-painting of Achilles killing the Amazon queen, Penthesileia. As she died, their eyes meet and (it was said) Achilles fell in love with her. Typical bloke. How would the following captions express that moment?\n(a) Ἀχιλλεὺς βλέψας πρὸς Πενθεσιλείαν ἐφλέγετο*.\n(b) Ἀχιλλεὺς βλέπων πρὸς Πενθεσιλείαν ἐφλέγετο.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
